    {
      "id": "F6",
      "statement": "Shared devices on A-9278's routes: device D-568 sent every route transfer from A-9278 (T0007, T0014), A-5092 (T0008, T0015) and A-2897 (T0009, T0016). Those are exactly the three route accounts that sent from D-568; A-4989 sent nothing in the dataset. None of the six senders of the contributing transfers uses a shared device.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "S1",
        "E7",
        "E8",
        "E9",
        "E10",
        "E11",
        "E12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F7",
      "statement": "Shared devices on A-9895's routes: no device was used by two or more of its route accounts (A-9895, A-1415). A-9895 sent T0041 from D-699 and A-1415 sent T0055 from D-785. The only other shared device in the dataset, D-619 (A-2952, A-9652), is not on either alert's routes.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "X1",
        "S2",
        "E19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F8",
      "statement": "What tells the alerts apart: as indicators they match (6 senders, 6 transfers, one hour each). The recorded relationships differ. (a) A-9278's chains are 3 links deep and pass through two intermediate accounts to one resting account; A-9895's chains are 1 link deep and go straight to A-1415. (b) All of A-9278's contributing transfers are passed on, but only half of A-9895's are. (c) The three accounts moving money along A-9278's route all sent from one device, D-568; A-9895's route has no shared device. (d) A-9278 received 357000 in varied amounts; A-9895 received 15000 in identical 2500 amounts. Only A-9278's alert combines layered onward movement with a common device across the route, so it calls for closer review. A-9895's alert, seen through these relationships alone, shows a shallow single pass-on.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "R1",
        "R2",
        "S1",
        "X1",
        "I1",
        "I2",
        "X5",
        "X6",
        "X7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F9",
      "statement": "The accounts where money comes to rest (A-4989, A-1415) and the intermediaries A-5092 and A-2897 have no fan-in alert of their own.",
